{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1155533-school-age-dragon-blooded-dynasty-campaign-ideas","id":1155533,"title":"School Age Dragon Blooded/Dynasty campaign ideas?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-03T14:08:46-07:00","id":1155533,"title":"School Age Dragon Blooded/Dynasty campaign ideas?","content":"I am planing a game set in a Realm Secondary School with un-Exalted Dynasty children. I would like to possibly infuse a Spirderman: Homecoming vibe into it.<br /> <br /> My time has been sorely stretched thine, &amp; I would love some helpful advice &amp; suggestions. Please feel free to pontificate and share at length.<br /> <br /> What type of challenges and intrigues could I breath into the story?<br /> <br /> I am tempted to have all the PC's be children of the Empress herself, to tie them together better and embroil them deeply in the intrigues. I haven't decided on the father(s), yet.<br /> <br /> I also want to emphasize the pressure on the children to Exalt.<br /> <br /> What House would you suggest for their PC's?<br /> <br /> Do you have any suggestions for NPC's?<br /> <br /> Thank you for your help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T17:49:56-07:00","id":1155600,"title":"","content":"So how light do you want this campaign to feel? Like do you want Spiderman: Homecoming style challenges where one of the characters has to work up the courage to go to a party? Or do you want it to really feel like the crushing claustrophobic sensation of being trapped in a school permanently with the massive pressure to exalt as well as excel?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T18:08:16-07:00","id":1155606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daredevil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1155533-school-age-dragon-blooded-dynasty-campaign-ideas#post1155533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am tempted to have all the PC's be children of the Empress herself, to tie them together better and embroil them deeply in the intrigues.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bBut that would mean that they all need to have different ages.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T18:14:25-07:00","id":1155609,"title":"","content":"I say just pick the school you want to run. The players can easily be from any house they want. If for some reason inter-house conflict keeps them from working together the instructors can easily force them to work together.<br /> <br /> What you really want is to ensure that NPCs all have differing loyalties. Some place the Realm first, others their house, some faith, some are totally selfish. You'll also want to ensure that the players feel the demands of loyalties and the conflicts that come with it.<br /> <br /> To apply pressure to exalt you simply need to award NPCs that Exalt. Use their exaltation to show favor. An NPC that was once considered a lost cause to family and the school, suddenly Exalting and becoming a favored child should show it well. Add even more if one of the players is from the same house. Take a benefit the player is receiving from the house and give it to the newly Exalted NPC.<br /> <br /> Beyond that a lot depends on a school the players will be attending. The Heptagram really lends itself to some Game of Thrones stuff, but you could change it around to have a more Harry Potter vibe to it. The House of Bells tends to be pretty serious, though it is great for buiding teamwork, but there are lots of older comedies that can be used as inspiration lighten up military training. I'm not so sure that you'll be able to get a Spiderman: Homecoming feel from the Cloister of Wisdom, given the strong religious focus, but you probably could focus more on the Martial Arts aspect and do emphasis the student Sifu relationship. The Spiral Academy probably fits a normal school environment the best, and has the advantage of being in the Imperial City allowing for all sorts of after school shenanigans, that said a school to train kids to be bureaucrats is kinda boring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T01:18:03-07:00","id":1155666,"title":"","content":"You might also consider primary schools, though that puts a cap on age of 15 (see Dragon-Blooded 2e page 20). That way, there's less stigma against being unExalted, and getting into the same secondary school could be a plot point for the campaign. Also, the schools are less 'themed' and more 'general', which may fit your characters better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T03:32:05-07:00","id":1155684,"title":"","content":"Try watching some animes. Specifically the ones about magical high schools (Asterix War, Akashic Record of the bastard instructor, etc). That gives a good source of ideas.<br /> <br /> Also, Mai-Hime and My-Otome, despite a more modern feel, work too. Hell, I want to do one with those characters someday. Just adjust them as they were adjusted between series","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T06:37:00-07:00","id":1155713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1155533-school-age-dragon-blooded-dynasty-campaign-ideas?p=1155600#post1155600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So how light do you want this campaign to feel? Like do you want Spiderman: Homecoming style challenges where one of the characters has to work up the courage to go to a party? Or do you want it to really feel like the crushing claustrophobic sensation of being trapped in a school permanently with the massive pressure to exalt as well as excel?</div> </div> </div> </div>Both. I'd like to turn up the heat &amp; then turn it more frivolous. Back &amp; forth. Peter Parker works up the courage to ask the amazing girl he has a crush on out to the dance. Then he stumbles into the truth of who the Vulture is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1155533-school-age-dragon-blooded-dynasty-campaign-ideas?p=1155606#post1155606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that would mean that they all need to have different ages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Magic could make them the same age. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Or natural quintuplets. I have a reason for her wanting a lot of children all of a sudden before her disappearance.<br /> <br /> I'm honestly surprised that the Dynasty (&amp; other DB groups) doesn\u2019t use magic to allow more mass births. It's hardly beyond the scope of 1st Circle Sorcery.<br /> <br /> The more I'm thinking about it, the more committed I am to use the Scarlet Empress as the mother.<br /> <br /> I've had a very different take on her disappearance, and this would make it more personal for the PC's &amp; allow me to add more weight if I get to the variant of the Empress' return I have in mind. Her disappearance will at least feel more urgent &amp; add to the sense of chaos &amp; foreboding.<br /> <br /> <br /> A big question I have is what kind of big threats should I have under the surface. Harry Potter has Voldemort. Buffy has villains of the week. What would be good for some initially un-Exalted Dynasts to handle???<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T06:47:15-07:00","id":1155718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daredevil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1155533-school-age-dragon-blooded-dynasty-campaign-ideas?p=1155713#post1155713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or natural quintuplets.</div> </div> </div> </div>With different fathers?<br /> <br /> \u200bI don't know; it's your game, it just seems an... odd detail.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daredevil</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm honestly surprised that the Dynasty (&amp; other DB groups) doesn\u2019t use magic to allow more mass births. It's hardly beyond the scope of 1st Circle Sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the developers of this Edition have resolved that question with the matter of how the heredity of Exaltation is limited and requires regeneration. You have a large number of children at once, you're still only getting one Exalt.<br /> <br /> Although even by the logic of prior Editions, the sheer burdensome expense of trying to bring up so many at once...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daredevil</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A big question I have is what kind of big threats should I have under the surface. Harry Potter has Voldemort. Buffy has villains of the week. What would be good for some initially un-Exalted Dynasts to handle???<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThe most straightforward answer is a scheming Dynast, but the next option I would think is a Lunar with a long-term agenda and who is keeping their cards close to their chest so that they don't draw a dangerous amount of attention from other Dragon Blooded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T07:58:46-07:00","id":1155729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1155533-school-age-dragon-blooded-dynasty-campaign-ideas?p=1155718#post1155718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With different fathers?.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s so unlikely that quintuplets would all Exalt that i\u2019d assume it\u2019s completely unprecedented, but it\u2019s still a matter of astronomical unlikelihood, not absolute impossibility. Player characters are allowed to be astronomically unlikely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T10:20:42-07:00","id":1155775,"title":"","content":"NPC wise I'd strongly suggest keeping away from Celestial Exalted until you're certain what you want the outcome of their inclusion to be. They're something that once the PCs interact with them its potentially going to change the game forever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T12:31:38-07:00","id":1155816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1155533-school-age-dragon-blooded-dynasty-campaign-ideas?p=1155718#post1155718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With different fathers?<br /> <br /> \u200bI don't know; it's your game, it just seems an... odd detail.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lol. I forgot I mentioned the possibility of different dad's. These posts are in the train of thought territory, and this is one has led to me verbally step in it quite a bit.<br /> <br /> Yes, if I stick with the Empress as mother/quintuplets idea it will be 1 father to avoid the creepy Jerry Springer vibe.<br /> <br /> NOW, IF IT WAS MY OLD GROUP OF PLAYERS, I'd totally do it. They had a weird sense of humor. My Lord, the hilarity.<br /> <br /> But it might also be better to have them be of different ages. I could have a role off to see who the oldest is. <i>Mu-wha, ha, ha, ha!</i><br /> <br /> I will respond more latter. Time crunch IRL.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T12:59:16-07:00","id":1155826,"title":"","content":"Having their mother be the Scarlet Empress, if this fact is widely known, would tend to imply that they're not part of any existing House. Which means that, with her gone, they basically have no support structure. There are enough people loyal to the Empress that their stipend and things they need for school will probably remain intact, but the institutional favoritism in the school is never going to benefit them and will usually work against them.<br /> <br /> If the Empress gave her children to various Houses to foster, with the implication that failing to keep the child safe would go poorly for them, the children will fare a little better as the Houses will still be supportive of them to a degree (because the Empress might still come back) but probably not as much as a native member of the house. House V'Neef is probably a good choice here. <br /> <br /> Either way, in 3e, a Dragon-Blooded parent can only confer the potential blessing of the dragons on their unborn child about once a decade or so. Which means that, whichever of the players Exalts first, everyone else will tend to assume the others are lost causes. Until they Exalt anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T13:03:04-07:00","id":1155828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daredevil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1155533-school-age-dragon-blooded-dynasty-campaign-ideas?p=1155816#post1155816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lol. I forgot I mentioned the possibility of different dad's. These posts are in the train of thought territory, and this is one has led to me verbally step in it quite a bit.<br /> <br /> Yes, if I stick with the Empress as mother/quintuplets idea it will be 1 father to avoid the creepy Jerry Springer vibe.<br /> <br /> NOW, IF IT WAS MY OLD GROUP OF PLAYERS, I'd totally do it. They had a weird sense of humor. My Lord, the hilarity.<br /> <br /> But it might also be better to have them be of different ages. I could have a role off to see who the oldest is. <i>Mu-wha, ha, ha, ha!</i><br /> <br /> I will respond more latter. Time crunch IRL.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I'd go with different fathers and have the children fostered with their father's houses. Neomah can totally handle that and, if the fathers are all DBs, then that sidesteps the assumption that only one of the children will Exalt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T17:19:59-07:00","id":1155894,"title":"","content":"Go play Persona 4. Then read Ender's Game and Ender's Shadow. Skip the rest of that series. Then watch Assassination Classroom, and add some New Mutants and Harry Potter to taste.<br /> <br /> These are the inspirations I am going to be using for my DB School Game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T18:43:21-07:00","id":1155912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daredevil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1155533-school-age-dragon-blooded-dynasty-campaign-ideas#post1155533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am planing a game set in a Realm Secondary School with un-Exalted Dynasty children. I would like to possibly infuse a Spirderman: Homecoming vibe into it.</div> </div> </div> </div>So... a dynast child who keeps their exaltation secret, sneaks off to fight crime in disguise, and is occasionally mentored by a mysterious warrior in face concealing power armour?<br /> <br /> Hmmm...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T20:59:44-07:00","id":1155934,"title":"","content":"I feel bad about having been down on the ideas before, so I want to adopt a more helpful and supportive stance.<br /> <br /> \u200bOne thing that occurred to me is that the figure of the Scarlet Empress, both in and out of character, is one who tends to accumulate a lot of mystery.<br /> <br /> \u200bI would find it to be in keeping with that for a number of characters of approximately the same age to come together, realise that each of them is a child of the Empress (with some or all of them having been raised with the statement that she was their mother, possibly even having occasionally been able to meet with her, but otherwise brought up under a cover story with surrogate parents), and then realising that that hardly makes any sense. They might speculate on whether it involved a particularly well kept secret of an unusually large pregnancy or some manner of weird sorcery, but there'll never really be anything that could reliably confirm one way or the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T15:46:59-08:00","id":1156179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1155533-school-age-dragon-blooded-dynasty-campaign-ideas?p=1155894#post1155894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Go play Persona 4. Then read Ender's Game</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, this inspired me. Dynast children must practice killing Anathema. There might be games &amp; play fights. Mock battles of victories past.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1155533-school-age-dragon-blooded-dynasty-campaign-ideas?p=1155894#post1155894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are the inspirations I am going to be using for my DB School Game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would love to hear more, if you care to share.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1155533-school-age-dragon-blooded-dynasty-campaign-ideas?p=1155912#post1155912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... a dynast child who keeps their exaltation secret, sneaks off to fight crime in disguise,</div> </div> </div> </div>Essential, yes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1155533-school-age-dragon-blooded-dynasty-campaign-ideas?p=1155912#post1155912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and is occasionally mentored by a mysterious warrior in face concealing power armour?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sh- I forgot about the mentor aspect. Thank you!<br /> <br /> You guys are really helping me think this through. Thank you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T19:00:47-08:00","id":1156218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1155533-school-age-dragon-blooded-dynasty-campaign-ideas?p=1155934#post1155934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThey might speculate on whether it involved a particularly well kept secret of an unusually large pregnancy or some manner of weird sorcery, but there'll never really be anything that could reliably confirm one way or the other.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absent a psychic vision coaxed from a tree, anyway. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T21:16:40-08:00","id":1156234,"title":"","content":"I just had a brainstorm for solving the OP's idea of the PCs all being children of the Empress.<br /> <br /> Have them all crwate their characters telling them that theirs is a child of the Empress (but dont tell them the othets are). When all find out, and realize it's impossible for them all to be and be the same age, this could be the set up for one of ylur story's long term plots.<br /> <br /> Now, just need to think of a sufgiciently cool explanation for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T17:14:02-08:00","id":1156518,"title":"","content":"Naruto actually has a great background for a DB-based school-like campaign setting.<br /> <br /> You can see elemental chakra specialty as aspect specialties, individual preference for Brawl, Melee or other forms of fighting, yet with a foundation level in use of Thrown. It does kind of fit well with the narrative that Dynastic children are given a really good broad-based education to equip them with as many skills as possible.<br /> <br /> So if you scale the elemental powers (hence Exaltation) back, you still have ninja kids who are broadly trained and kinda ready for combat. And only when they receive the Second Breath do they technically start learning to use their Essence (chakra)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21242-charonferryman","name":"CharonFerryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21242_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T18:47:37-08:00","id":1156535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1155533-school-age-dragon-blooded-dynasty-campaign-ideas?p=1156234#post1156234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just had a brainstorm for solving the OP's idea of the PCs all being children of the Empress.<br /> <br /> Have them all crwate their characters <b>telling them that theirs is a child of the Empress</b> (<b>but dont tell them the othets are</b>). <b>When all find out, and realize it's impossible for them all to be and be the same age</b>, this could be the set up for one of ylur story's long term plots.<br /> <br /> Now, just need to think of a sufgiciently cool explanation for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotchas can be fun, but I wouldn't suggest springing it on a group if you don't know the players well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T10:23:03-08:00","id":1157046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1155533-school-age-dragon-blooded-dynasty-campaign-ideas?p=1155934#post1155934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> One thing that occurred to me is that the figure of the Scarlet Empress, both in and out of character, is one who tends to accumulate a lot of mystery.<br /> <br /> \u200bI would find it to be in keeping with that for a number of characters of approximately the same age to come together, realise that each of them is a child of the Empress (with some or all of them having been raised with the statement that she was their mother, possibly even having occasionally been able to meet with her, but otherwise brought up under a cover story with surrogate parents), and then realising that that hardly makes any sense. They might speculate on whether it involved a particularly well kept secret of an unusually large pregnancy or some manner of weird sorcery, but there'll never really be anything that could reliably confirm one way or the other.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mystery does a lot to keep Players glued &amp; invested. I was originally going to have them share the secret (if it is a secret) to bind them together as a group. The angle of discovering they are all siblings in character might be a lot of fun, though.<br /> <br /> And there will be an even bigger secret they will have to keep latter one. This could foreshadow it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1155533-school-age-dragon-blooded-dynasty-campaign-ideas?p=1156234#post1156234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have them all crwate their characters telling them that theirs is a child of the Empress (but dont tell them the othets are). When all find out, and realize it's impossible for them all to be and be the same age, this could be the set up for one of ylur story's long term plots.<br /> <br /> Now, just need to think of a sufgiciently cool explanation for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps I should do the secret mother angle. It seem to capture people's imagination.<br /> <br /> But I might be focusing on the parentage angle a bit too much.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>I could really use some inspiration for the more active cast &amp; setting.</b><br /> <br /> Do you have any suggestions for fellow students they can interact with?<br /> <br /> What types of teachers could be useful &amp; entertaining? One MUST be a villain/antagonist in disguise. But what about the others?<br /> <br /> What types of classes &amp; activities would be good for this type of story???<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4428,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","user":"Daredevil","date":". 11-08-2017, 01:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T10:25:19-08:00","id":1157048,"title":"","content":"&lt;&lt;Double Post. Please delete.&gt;&gt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T17:37:20-08:00","id":1160058,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial, sans-serif\">Disclaimer: I did not read the thread. Apologies for redundant ideas.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial, sans-serif\">That being said, I love the OP's idea. Page 287 of First Edition's Exalted: The Dragon-Blooded has rules for playing as children and even has some \u201cBoarding School Story Ideas.\u201d If you have access to that book I highly recommend giving it a look (I'd quote stuff, but don't remember the forum rules on doing that :/ ).</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial, sans-serif\">Here's some of my story seeds.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial, sans-serif\">One of the PCs' peers secretly exalts. This former bullied underdog, uses his newfound abilities without expending peripheral essence in order to exact his/her revenge. How will the PCs react if they realize what's going on?</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial, sans-serif\">One of PCs romantic interests (who was not likely to exalt) suddenly exalts in the middle of an intense sports competition between houses. In this sudden unexpected dramatic event, school officials immediately intervene and sequester the new exalt from the PCs. As the new exalt is being hurried away (drug away kicking and screaming according to the perception of the PC children) from the mortals (anima flux is hazardous after all) he/she struggles to stay with the only real friends (and romantic interest) he/she could trust.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial, sans-serif\">One of the instructors is known to be incredibly kind. He/she is a favorite amongst the students. The PCs come across information that alleges the instructor has an incredibly dark secret. Perhaps the PCs' rivals are trying to undermine/blackmail the instructor or get the instructor terminated.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial, sans-serif\">You could Harry Potter it up with dividing the primary school into different made up \u201cHouses\u201d to kind of microcosm simulate Realm society. The PCs' rival House's faculty sponsor hates the PCs' House and the PCs in particular for some reason. The PCs resolve to find out why and possibly attempt to get the faculty member canned.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial, sans-serif\">That's all I got at the moment.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}